@startuml
title Sequence Diagram - Refund a Failed Payment
autonumber

actor Customer
participant "PayLink App" as App
participant "Payment Module" as Payment
participant "Biller Integration" as BillerInt
participant "External Biller" as Biller
participant "Accounts & Wallet" as Wallet
participant "Notifications" as Notif

note over Payment : State: FundsHeld

Payment -> BillerInt : Send payment request
note over Payment : State: SentToBiller
BillerInt -> Biller : Pay bill

alt Immediate Biller Refusal
    Biller --> BillerInt : Refused (Error code)
    BillerInt --> Payment : Payment refused
else Timeout followed by Retry/Callback Refusal
    Biller --x BillerInt : No response (Timeout)
    BillerInt --> Payment : Timeout
    note over Payment : State: Unknown (Funds remain held)
    
    BillerInt -> Biller : Re-query payment status
    Biller --> BillerInt : Refused / Not received
    BillerInt --> Payment : Confirmed failure
end

== Refund Process ==
note over Payment : State: Failed
Payment -> Wallet : Release held funds back to available balance
Wallet --> Payment : Hold released (Refund ledger entry created)
note over Payment : State: Refunded

Payment -> Notif : Send failure & refund notice (SMS & Push)
Notif --> Customer : Receive failure reason & refund confirmation
Payment --> App : Display payment failed & refunded
@enduml